  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the extracted `CommunicationAttachmentsService.ts` + `AttachmentApiService.ts`, when grepped, then neither contains `import ... from 'react'` (React-agnostic adapters, NFR-05); the promoted `AttachmentList` uses no React-18/19-only runtime API and no `as React.ComponentType` cast.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the `CommunicationAttachments` PCF, when built with `npm run build:prod`, then it compiles clean importing `AttachmentList` + services from `@spaarke/communication-components`, its local duplicates are deleted, and its React 16 view is unchanged (regression-free, NFR-04).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a mixed attachment set, when the list renders, then inline-image attachment types are filtered out and remaining files list with type labels (FR-12) — behavior identical to pre-extraction.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an attachment row click, when activated, then the REUSED `RichFilePreviewDialog` from `@spaarke/ui-components` opens (no forked preview dialog).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the shared barrel, when imported, then it re-exports the attachments core + adapters without disturbing the connections export from task 020; no business logic is duplicated between PCF and shared lib.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: `AttachmentApiService` issues its BFF calls via `authenticatedFetch` (ADR-028) — grep confirms no raw `fetch(` to the document endpoints and no client-supplied identity.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Shared lib build + PCF `build:prod` both green; existing `CommunicationAttachments` unit tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Cite spec FR-18 + FR-12 + NFR-04 + NFR-05 in the PR. EXTRACTION of existing code (COMPLETE-class) — no §11 `&lt;justification&gt;` (modify/refactor exempt). Barrel edits serialize with 022 — coordinate the `src/index.ts` edit. Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `@spaarke/communication-components`, contended with messaging-r2/r3, notification-spine-r1, email-r4). Completion summary appended here when done.</notes>

